+# Before vs After: Record Injection Accessibility
+
+## Before: Hook-Based Only
+
+```
+Hook-enabled editors/agents
+        ↓
+  onPreToolUse hook
+        ↓
+  Records injected
+        ↓
+    User sees context
+
+
+Hook-unsupported editors/agents
+        ↓
+    (no hook)
+        ↓
+  NO records injected
+        ↓
+  User sees nothing ❌
+```
+
+**Coverage**: ~50% of team (those with hook support)
+
+**Problem**: Half the team gets no records at all.
+
+---
+
+## After: Universal API + Hook
+
+```
+Hook-enabled editors/agents          Hook-unsupported editors/agents
+        ↓                                     ↓
+  onPreToolUse hook                   getContext(repo, filePath)
+        ↓                                     ↓
+  Records injected                    Records available
+        ↓                                     ↓
+  User sees context ✓                 User sees context ✓
+
+
+All agents reading files
+        ↓
+readWithContext() wrapper
+        ↓
+Auto-inject records if available
+        ↓
+User sees context ✓
+```
+
+**Coverage**: 100% of team
+
+**How**: 
+1. Hook users get fast pre-tool injection (unchanged)
+2. Hookless users call `getContext()` or use `readWithContext()` 
+3. Both use the same underlying store (path-scoped, no bloat)
+
+---
+
+## Concrete Examples
+
+### User A (VS Code with plugin, has hook support)
+
+**Before & After (same)**:
+```typescript
+const filePath = "src/core/query.ts";
+// Editor calls onPreToolUse(repo, filePath)
+// → Hook injects context automatically
+// → User sees context in editor
+```
+
+### User B (Custom agent, no hook support)
+
+**Before**:
+```typescript
+const filePath = "src/core/query.ts";
+// No hook → no records → nothing to show
+// User is left in the dark
+```
+
+**After**:
+```typescript
+const filePath = "src/core/query.ts";
+
+// Option 1: Explicit fetching
+const context = getContext(repo, filePath);
+if (context) {
+  // Append to response
+}
+
+// Option 2: Automatic injection
+const result = readWithContext({ repo, filePath });
+// result.context contains records if available
+```
+
+### User C (CLI-based editor)
+
+**Before**: No context
+
+**After**:
+```bash
+# New CLI command, accessible from any editor
+commitlore-context --repo=/path/to/repo --file=src/core/query.ts
+
+# Or via HTTP (language server)
+curl "http://localhost:9000/context?repo=/path/to/repo&file=src/core/query.ts"
+```
+
+---
+
+## Key Properties Preserved
+
+| Property | Before | After |
+|----------|--------|-------|
+| **Path scoping** | ✓ One path → one set of records | ✓ Same, via store index |
+| **Performance** | ✓ O(1) on hook call | ✓ O(1) on API call |
+| **No stale files** | ✓ In-memory, loaded fresh | ✓ Same, via loader pattern |
+| **No session bloat** | ✓ Lazy-loaded per path | ✓ Same, lazy store population |
+| **Backward compat** | N/A | ✓ Hook still works for old users |
+
+---
+
+## Migration Checklist
+
+- [ ] Implement `Store` (in-memory index by path)
+- [ ] Implement `Loader` (pluggable record sources)
+- [ ] Implement public API (`getContext`, `readWithContext`)
+- [ ] Update hook to use `Store` (optional optimization)
+- [ ] Document public API usage patterns
+- [ ] Create CLI/HTTP endpoint for non-agent users
+- [ ] Migrate custom agents to use `getContext()` or `readWithContext()`
+- [ ] Deprecate hook once all users switch (optional, can keep both)
